    "user_request_original": "Design a 16-layer periodic dielectric stack on CaF2 substrate for mid-IR dual-band pass filter. Stack topology: Air | ThSi2 | YbF3 | ThSi2 | YbF3 | ThSi2 | YbF3 | ThSi2 | YbF3 | ThSi2 | YbF3 | ThSi2 | YbF3 | ThSi2 | YbF3 | ThSi2 | YbF3 | CaF2. Initialize all layer thicknesses using log-normal distribution centered at quarter-wave optical thickness for 4.45 μm (ThSi2 ~370 nm, YbF3 ~740 nm assuming n_H=3.0, n_L=1.5) with σ=0.15. Enforce hard minimum thickness 6.0 nm per layer and maximum 800 nm per layer. Wavelength range: 3600-5200 nm. Angle: 0 degrees (normal incidence). Polarization: unpolarized. Optimize 16 thickness variables to maximize mean transmittance in passbands (4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm) and minimize mean transmittance in stopbands (3600-4000 nm, 4850-5200 nm). Use coherent TMM with smatrix. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 16 thickness variables in an Air | ThSi2 | YbF3 alternating stack on a CaF2 substrate for normal-incidence unpolarized light from 3600 to 5200 nm, maximizing mean transmittance in 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm while minimizing it in 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm, subject to 6–800 nm layer thickness bounds.",
